      },
      "facts": {
        "decisive-excerpt": {
          "text": "In a two sector model, there are two sources of final demand, the first is consumption and the second is investment. The investment function was shown as I = I Graphically, this is shown as a horizontal line at a height equal to I above the horizontal axis. In this model, I is autonomous which means, it is the same no matter whatever is the level of income."
