      },
      "facts": {
        "decisive-excerpt": {
          "text": "Thumbs move like skilled pianists, but the true rhythm of life remains unheard amid the dissonance of digital noise. Constant connectivity creates a hunch on shoulders, a physical sign of the burden of information overload. Minds stay alert for the next like, share or comment.\n\n(4) Despite efforts to stay connected, people become increasingly isolated among digital faces. Genuine connections are fleeting amid the constant clamour for attention. The search for digital validation sacrifices meaningful moments and shared experiences."
        }
      },
      "supports": {
        "decisive-excerpt": "85354ebb8fe83119b4b58e70d92c1c06b5921c3facd43d23b676ad3296957ce1"
      },
